  "body": "With Settings → \"Detect agents in WSL\" turned off (`noWSLAgents: true`), every Claude request still reaches `wsl.exe` through the stand-in/classifier hot path — bypassing the guards on `wslrun.Find`, `wslAgents`, and `checkSides`.\n\nOn a machine with no WSL installed, Windows' inbox `wsl.exe` answers each of those calls with a console window asking to install WSL. The popup fires on every Claude request, so the user sees it recur constantly.\n\n**Root cause:** `wslReady` and `wslClaudeClassifier` (internal/agent/wsl.go) call `wslRunningLocked()` → `wslList(\"-l\",\"--running\",\"-q\")` → `wslRun` → `wsl.exe` without checking `wslLooks()` (the `NoWSLAgents` gate used elsewhere).\n\n`wslReady` also serves `wslClaudeStandIn` and `wslCodexStandIn`, so gating it fixes all three.\n\n**Patch attached.** Verified on Windows 11 with `noWSLAgents: true`: `wsl.exe` is no longer started. A regression test (`TestWSLStandInAsksNothingWhenOff`) is included in the patch.\n\nThe change is also on a branch at `OldKing-lion/magpie:wsl-standin-gate` if that helps review.\n\n<!-- Failed to upload \"wsl-gate.patch\" -->",
