   "body": "A request's stand-in and classifier paths asked `wsl.exe` on their own, past the `NoWSLAgents` gate (#4872, follow-up to #1264).\n\n**Symptom**: with Settings → Detect agents in WSL off, every Claude request still launched `wsl.exe`; on a machine with no WSL installed, Windows' inbox `wsl.exe` answers each of those with a console window asking to install WSL, so the popup recurs on every request.\n\n**Root cause**: `wslReady` (which serves `wslClaudeStandIn` and `wslCodexStandIn`) and `wslClaudeClassifier` (`internal/agent/wsl.go`) call `wslRunningLocked()` → `wslList(\"-l\",\"--running\",\"-q\")` → `wsl.exe` without checking `wslLooks()` — the gate #1264 put on `wslAgents`, `wslHomes` and `WSLRunning`. The gateway asks the stand-ins per request (`StandIn` and `ClassifierStandIn`), so the asks recur.\n\n**Fix**: both read `wslLooks()` first, as the rest of WSL's own asks do. Detection off, a request's stand-in finds no distro and asks wsl.exe nothing; detection on, everything works as before. `fakeWSL` (the test helper) now sets `wslOn`, as `FakeWSL` already does, since the stand-in paths it exercises are gated on `wslLooks`.\n\n**Verification** (base `c86fa2a34`, head `81745f4a7`):\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Red without the fix (`TestWSLStandInAsksNothingWhenOff`, `wsl.go` reverted, tests kept) | `--- FAIL: TestWSLStandInAsksNothingWhenOff — wsl.exe asked with detection off: [\"-l --running -q\" \"-l --running -q\" \"-l --running -q\"]` — once per path |\n| Green with the fix | `ok` |\n| Neighbors | `TestWSLClaudeStandIn`, `TestWSLCodexStandIn` (+`SkipsStopped`), `TestWSLDetectionOff`, `TestWSLCodexBaseURL`, the WSL suite: `ok` |\n| `go test ./internal/agent -count=1` | one red, `TestDshACPSettingsGetTheRoute` — the same red on bare `main` on this machine (its 0644 expectation against a 0027 umask), not from this change |\n| `gofmt -l`, `go vet -tags nogui`, `go build -tags nogui` (darwin, GOOS=linux, GOOS=windows) | clean / clean / ok |\n\n**Not verified**: the real Windows popup — the test asserts the spawn-command level (wsl.exe asked nothing); the reporter's install-prompt observation is their own machine's.\n\n---\n\n**Attribution**: AI-written; I've read the whole diff and the tests pass. Please keep the author (`vincent`) or add `Co-authored-by: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>`.\n\n**Branch with the commit**: [`fix/4872-wsl-standin-gate`](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/4872-wsl-standin-gate) (head `81745f4a7`).\n",
