   "updated_at": "2026-11-06T13:30:54Z",
   "body": "Fixed in **v0.1.3176** (f4068ccc2). Keeping this open until the reporter confirms the popup is gone.\n\nWith Settings → Detect agents in WSL off, magpie no longer starts wsl.exe on any path. The gate sits in `proc`, where every command magpie runs is made: `proc.Command`, `CommandContext` and `ProbeContext` refuse wsl.exe, under any name or path, with `proc.ErrWSLOff` (`internal/proc/wsl.go`). That covers the stand-in and classifier paths this issue found, and also the other wsl.exe paths that skipped the #1264 gate: agent's `wslRun`/`wslExec`, `wslrun.Run`/`In`/`Up`/`Stop` and Tool commands, library's cmdvars/mcp_wsl/rtk_wsl, claudetui's wslread, and the Claude TUI helper's ConPTY start. @skygunner's stand-in fix (vincent) is in the same commit and credited. It makes those paths return early, before they take wsl's lock.\n\nRun:\n- mote: `go vet` darwin, plus `GOOS=windows` and `GOOS=linux` vet of proc, agent, wslrun, claudetui (library and gateway on windows too): clean. `go test ./internal/proc ./internal/wslrun ./internal/claudetui`: ok. `-run 'WSL|Wsl|Dsh'` on agent, library, sessions: ok. Proc, wslrun and agent's WSL tests ran again at the pushed head: ok.\n- Windows 11 (xiaomi-gpu, win-run): the new tests `TestWSLOffStartsNoWSL`, `TestWSLRunnerRefusedWhenOff` (agent's real `wslRun`), `TestRunRefusedWhenOff` and `TestWSLStandInAsksNothingWhenOff`, with `TestWSLDetectionOff`, `TestWSLClaudeStandIn`, `TestWSLCodexStandIn` and `TestNoCommandBypassesProc`: ok. Whole `./internal/proc` and `./internal/wslrun`: ok.\n- Broken by hand (proc's check disabled, agent/wsl.go at origin/main): all four new tests went red, and the stand-in test recorded three `-l --running -q` asks.\n\nNot tried: a Windows machine without WSL (the install window itself). The full suite is running under the lock now, and anything red from it will be filed.\n",
   "author_association": "OWNER",
